			],
			"Message": "build(Sky): Enforce source-based VSCode compilation and add .gitignore\n\nThis commit removes the fallback path to the prebuilt Microsoft Editor output in CopyVSCode.js, ensuring that Sky now exclusively uses the compiled VSCode artifacts from the Output package (built via Rest compiler). This enforces the source-based compilation pipeline and removes the implicit dependency on the raw Dependency/Editor/out directory.\n\nAdditionally, a comprehensive .gitignore file is added to the Sky project to exclude ephemeral build artifacts (Target/, Configuration/), Astro cache, environment files, logs, and IDE configurations, while preserving the dev server certificates.\n\nImpact: Ensures consistent build behavior by routing all VSCode asset loading through the Land build pipeline (Rest -> Output) rather than allowing fallback to upstream prebuilt artifacts.",
			"SHA": "dcd5ba528c217f9904e4adc52e196c498bcbdbfc"
